<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>HJPARAM Article Manuscript Template</title>
<!--[if gte mso 9]>
<xml>
<w:WordDocument>
<w:View>Print</w:View>
<w:Zoom>100</w:Zoom>
<w:DoNotOptimizeForBrowser/>
</w:WordDocument>
</xml>
<![endif]-->
<style>
body {
    font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;
    font-size: 11pt;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: #1e293b;
    margin: 1in;
}
.journal-header {
    border-bottom: 2pt solid #0284c7;
    padding-bottom: 6pt;
    margin-bottom: 18pt;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
}
.journal-title {
    font-size: 10pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #0369a1;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
}
.manuscript-type {
    font-size: 9.5pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #64748b;
    text-transform: uppercase;
}
h1.article-title {
    font-size: 18pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    line-height: 1.25;
    color: #0f172a;
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 12pt;
}
.author-names {
    font-size: 12pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #1e293b;
    margin-bottom: 4pt;
}
.author-affiliations {
    font-size: 9.5pt;
    color: #475569;
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin-bottom: 12pt;
}
.corresponding-info {
    font-size: 9.5pt;
    color: #0369a1;
    border-top: 1pt solid #e2e8f0;
    border-bottom: 1pt solid #e2e8f0;
    padding: 4pt 0;
    margin-bottom: 16pt;
}
.abstract-box {
    background-color: #f8fafc;
    border-left: 3pt solid #0284c7;
    padding: 10pt 14pt;
    margin-bottom: 18pt;
}
.abstract-title {
    font-size: 11pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #0f172a;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 4pt;
}
.abstract-text {
    font-size: 10pt;
    text-align: justify;
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin-bottom: 6pt;
}
.keywords-text {
    font-size: 10pt;
    color: #334155;
}
h2.heading {
    font-size: 13pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #0f172a;
    border-bottom: 1pt solid #e2e8f0;
    padding-bottom: 2pt;
    margin-top: 16pt;
    margin-bottom: 8pt;
}
h3.subheading {
    font-size: 11pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #334155;
    margin-top: 10pt;
    margin-bottom: 4pt;
}
p.body-text {
    font-size: 11pt;
    text-align: justify;
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 10pt;
}
table.data-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 14pt 0;
}
table.data-table th, table.data-table td {
    border-top: 1pt solid #000;
    border-bottom: 1pt solid #000;
    padding: 5pt 8pt;
    font-size: 9.5pt;
    text-align: left;
}
table.data-table th {
    font-weight: bold;
    background-color: #f8fafc;
    border-bottom: 1.5pt solid #000;
}
.table-caption {
    font-size: 9.5pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-bottom: 4pt;
}
.figure-box {
    border: 1pt dashed #94a3b8;
    background-color: #f8fafc;
    padding: 20pt;
    text-align: center;
    margin: 14pt 0;
}
.figure-caption {
    font-size: 9.5pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: left;
    margin-top: 4pt;
}
.ref-item {
    font-size: 9.5pt;
    text-indent: -20pt;
    padding-left: 20pt;
    margin-bottom: 6pt;
    text-align: justify;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="journal-header">
    <div class="journal-title">HJPARAM PUBLICATION • OFFICIAL MANUSCRIPT TEMPLATE</div>
    <div class="manuscript-type">Original Research Article</div>
</div>

<h1 class="article-title">Concise, Descriptive Title of Your Research Article in Title Case Format</h1>

<div class="author-names">
    Firstname A. Author<sup>1,*</sup>, Secondname B. Co-Author<sup>2</sup>, and Thirdname C. Senior-Author<sup>1,3</sup>
</div>

<div class="author-affiliations">
    <sup>1</sup> Department of Advanced Computing, University Institute of Technology, City, Country<br>
    <sup>2</sup> Laboratory for Applied Nanotechnology & Materials, Research Academy, City, Country<br>
    <sup>3</sup> Centre for Interdisciplinary Life Sciences, Metropolitan University, City, Country
</div>

<div class="corresponding-info">
    * <strong>Corresponding Author:</strong> Firstname A. Author | Email: corresponding.author@university.edu | ORCID: 0000-0000-0000-0000
</div>

<div class="abstract-box">
    <div class="abstract-title">Abstract</div>
    <p class="abstract-text">
        <strong>Background:</strong> Provide a concise context explaining the problem, scientific rationale, and overarching hypothesis of the investigation (approximately 50 words). 
        <strong>Methods:</strong> Detail the primary experimental methodology, study design, algorithms, sample cohort, or analytical parameters applied (approx. 70 words). 
        <strong>Results:</strong> State the core quantitative and qualitative findings, including key statistical metrics, percentages, p-values, or performance benchmarks (approx. 80 words). 
        <strong>Conclusion:</strong> Summarize the direct contribution to the scholarly body of knowledge and future research trajectory (approx. 50 words). Total abstract must not exceed 250 words without citations.
    </p>
    <div class="keywords-text">
        <strong>Keywords:</strong> Manuscript Template; Peer Review; Scientific Methodology; Open Access; Data Analysis (4 to 6 keywords separated by semicolons)
    </div>
</div>

<h2 class="heading">1. Introduction</h2>
<p class="body-text">
    The introduction should provide an authoritative overview of the current scientific context, state of the art, and existing research gaps. Cite recent, peer-reviewed literature to justify the novelty and necessity of your study [1, 2]. Avoid an exhaustive historical review; instead, focus directly on the questions addressed in this manuscript. State the explicit hypotheses and specific objectives clearly at the end of this section.
</p>

<h2 class="heading">2. Materials and Methods</h2>
<p class="body-text">
    Methodological descriptions must provide sufficient technical detail to enable independent researchers to reproduce the experimental or theoretical findings. Standard procedures should be cited concisely, while novel modifications must be articulated comprehensively.
</p>

<h3 class="subheading">2.1. Ethical Clearances and Sample Acquisition</h3>
<p class="body-text">
    For investigations involving human participants or animal subjects, include an explicit ethical declaration specifying the approving Institutional Review Board (IRB) or Animal Ethics Committee alongside the formal approval protocol ID. State that informed consent was obtained in writing.
</p>

<h3 class="subheading">2.2. Experimental Design and Statistical Framework</h3>
<p class="body-text">
    Specify analytical instrumentation (manufacturer, city, country), reagent purity, computational frameworks, and statistical software packages (e.g., SPSS, R, Python NumPy/SciPy). Clearly define threshold significance levels (e.g., p &lt; 0.05).
</p>

<h2 class="heading">3. Results</h2>
<p class="body-text">
    Present empirical findings sequentially in logical text, tables, and high-resolution figures. Do not duplicate tabular data in running prose; highlight key trends, anomalies, and statistically significant variances.
</p>

<div class="table-caption">Table 1. Experimental performance comparison between proposed methodology and baseline benchmarks.</div>
<table class="data-table">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Experimental Group</th>
            <th>Sample Size (N)</th>
            <th>Accuracy (%)</th>
            <th>Latency (ms)</th>
            <th>p-value</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>Baseline Model A</td>
            <td>150</td>
            <td>84.3 ± 1.2</td>
            <td>42.5 ± 2.1</td>
            <td>-</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Baseline Model B</td>
            <td>150</td>
            <td>89.1 ± 0.9</td>
            <td>38.2 ± 1.8</td>
            <td>0.034</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Proposed Framework</strong></td>
            <td><strong>150</strong></td>
            <td><strong>96.7 ± 0.4</strong></td>
            <td><strong>21.6 ± 1.1</strong></td>
            <td><strong>&lt; 0.001*</strong></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<div class="figure-box">
    [INSERT HIGH-RESOLUTION FIGURE HERE (Min. 300 DPI, TIFF / PNG / JPEG Format)]
</div>
<div class="figure-caption">Figure 1. Architectural schema and comparative validation trajectory of the experimental workflow.</div>

<h2 class="heading">4. Discussion</h2>
<p class="body-text">
    Interpret your findings in the broader context of existing published studies. Discuss theoretical implications, potential mechanisms, unexpected outcomes, and methodological limitations. Emphasize how your data corroborates or challenges prevailing scientific dogmas [3].
</p>

<h2 class="heading">5. Conclusions</h2>
<p class="body-text">
    Highlight the primary conclusions and prospective translational applications emerging from the study. Avoid restating the abstract; instead, summarize the overarching takeaways and articulate future research directions.
</p>

<h2 class="heading">Declarations & Statements</h2>
<p class="body-text"><strong>Author Contributions:</strong> Conceptualization, F.A.A. and T.C.S.; methodology, S.B.C.; validation, F.A.A. and S.B.C.; formal analysis, F.A.A.; investigation, S.B.C.; writing—original draft preparation, F.A.A.; writing—review and editing, T.C.S.; supervision, T.C.S. All authors have read and agreed to the published version of the manuscript.</p>
<p class="body-text"><strong>Funding:</strong> This research received external funding from [Grant Agency Name, Grant ID: #########]. If no external funding was received, state: "This research received no external funding."</p>
<p class="body-text"><strong>Institutional Review Board Statement:</strong> The study was conducted in accordance with the Declaration of Helsinki, and approved by the Ethics Committee of [Institution Name] (Protocol Code: #######, Date: DD/MM/YYYY).</p>
<p class="body-text"><strong>Informed Consent Statement:</strong> Informed consent was obtained from all subjects involved in the study.</p>
<p class="body-text"><strong>Data Availability Statement:</strong> The raw datasets generated and analyzed during the current study are available in the [Repository Name] repository at [Persistent DOI / URL Link].</p>
<p class="body-text"><strong>Conflicts of Interest:</strong> The authors declare no conflict of interest.</p>

<h2 class="heading">References</h2>
<div class="ref-item">[1] Smith, J. K., &amp; Williams, R. (2024). Advanced computational paradigms in peer-reviewed scientific publishing. <em>Journal of Academic Innovations</em>, 12(3), 145-160. https://doi.org/10.xxxx/jai.2024.123</div>
<div class="ref-item">[2] Johnson, M. L., Patel, D. A., &amp; Kumar, S. (2025). Digital preservation frameworks for open access scholarship. <em>Scholarly Publishing Review</em>, 8(1), 22-37.</div>
<div class="ref-item">[3] Anderson, P. (2023). <em>Statistical Methods in Modern Research Design</em> (2nd ed.). Academic Press, New York.</div>

</body>
</html>
